 ## Overview
-The Visual Complexity (VC) algorithm is a non-photorealistic volume rendering technique that simulates the local visual variations found in hand-painted artworks to enhance aesthetic judgment and detail perception [S1]. Unlike Interpretational Complexity (IC), which establishes global trends across the volume, VC focuses on local variations in stroke properties such as color, thickness, and contour to create a dense, textured appearance [S1]. It differs from [Interactive Volume Illustration (Hatching)](5272-interactive-volume-illustration-hatching.md) by employing a single-region, full-coverage painting strategy with varied stroke geometries rather than structured hatching lines, and from [Fast Paint Texture](14343-fast-paint-texture.md) by integrating embossing as a post-processing lighting effect on 2D stroke textures rather than a primary geometric modeling step.
