 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity**: The painting loop runs until coverage $V_k$ is met. The number of strokes is proportional to the area of $S_k$ divided by the average stroke area. Each stroke requires sampling and geometric computation.
-*   **Memory Complexity**: Linear in the number of strokes, storing geometry, color, and texture references.
-*   **Performance**: The use of 2D textured quads and Bézier curves is computationally cheaper than full 3D mesh modeling. Embossing adds a lighting pass but avoids expensive 3D geometry.
-*   **Strengths**: Produces aesthetically pleasing, hand-painted look; handles local data variations well; efficient compared to 3D NPR.
-*   **Limitations**: Coverage control can be slow if strokes are large or regions are complex; requires pre-scanned textures; not physically based.
